<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    PowerFramework.Shared.Localization
    ==================================

    Shared library: the I18N translation surface and its three locale providers. One of the six
    shared libraries under shared/ (Kernel, Diagnostics, Eventful, Localization, Containers,
    Contracts) that sit BENEATH the four Phase 1 services. AAP §0.1.5 requires that layer to carry
    "only pure behaviour and no I/O": no host, no socket, no endpoint, no database, and nothing here
    listens or dials out.

    That rule has exactly ONE narrow exception, stated plainly rather than glossed over, because the
    file list below would otherwise contradict it: I18nResourceReader.cs READS the pfw.i18n.xml
    translation table from disk. It is an exception the AAP itself mandates and not a liberty taken
    here. AAP §0.2.1.3 Correction 6 requires the legacy n_xmldoc load to be SUBSTITUTED with
    System.Xml.Linq.XDocument.Load, so some read has to happen somewhere, and the legacy performs it
    inside these very providers. It stays within the spirit of the rule: read only, local, no write
    path, and no listener or outbound connection of any kind. Which is precisely why localization
    remains a shared LIBRARY and does not become a service.

    WHY THIS IS A SHARED LIBRARY AND NOT A SERVICE
    Localization is a confirmed requirement rather than a conditional one (AAP §0.1.4): the
    DataWindow validation path calls I18N(ne_cst_i18n.CAT_DWSVC, ...) directly at
    ws_objects/pfw.datawindow.services.pbl.src/se_cst_dw.sru:L357 and :L368, and CAT_DWSVC is
    consumed by three in scope objects. It is therefore reached by more than one Phase 1 service and
    can belong to none of them. It is also NOT one of the eight target services: AAP §0.8.3
    Deviation 1 records that the environment's "localization-service" directory is a placeholder
    whose capability content maps to a shared LIBRARY, not to a service, so no such service exists
    and none may be created.

    Legacy sources ported into this folder, per AAP §0.3.1 and §0.4.2.3:

        II18nProvider.cs                  ws_objects/pfw.ui.pbl.src/n_cst_i18n.sru
                                          One member, ontranslate(source, category, ref text):
                                          translation MUTATES a ref string, it does not return a
                                          value.
        I18n.cs                           ws_objects/pfw.ui.pbl.src/i18n.srf
                                          Three overloads. Preserves the SILENT PASSTHROUGH
                                          fallback: with no provider installed the text is returned
                                          unchanged, and it must never throw, never log and never
                                          mark the text untranslated.
        Categories.cs                     ws_objects/pfw.ui.controls.ext.pbl.src/ne_cst_i18n.sru
                                          :L16-L17. CAT_MSGBOX and CAT_DWSVC as offsets from
                                          I18N_CAT_CUSTOM.
        EnglishProvider.cs                ws_objects/pfw.ui.controls.ext.pbl.src/n_cst_i18n_en.sru
                                          Reproduces BOTH mistranslations. The commented out pre XML
                                          table at :L58-L153 holds the CORRECT wording and must NOT
                                          be revived: reviving it is the silent correction AAP
                                          §0.8.2 forbids.
        SimplifiedChineseProvider.cs      ws_objects/pfw.ui.controls.ext.pbl.src/n_cst_i18n_chs.sru
                                          A genuine no op, because Simplified Chinese is the base
                                          locale. The three provider shape is reproduced including
                                          this one.
        TraditionalChineseProvider.cs     ws_objects/pfw.ui.controls.ext.pbl.src/n_cst_i18n_cht.sru
        I18nResourceReader.cs             pfw.i18n.xml, read at n_cst_i18n_en.sru:L158-L159 and
                                          n_cst_i18n_cht.sru:L62-L63.

    THE LEGACY TREE IS READ ONLY (AAP §0.7.3 C-C) AND SHARES THIS WORKING DIRECTORY
    The .sru paths above are the behavioural oracle: read as specification, never edited, moved or
    reformatted, and never a build input. Nothing under ws_objects/ and no *.pbl, *.pbt, *.pbw,
    *.pbr or *.pbd is compiled or embedded here, which is why no ItemGroup below names a legacy
    path. The root .dockerignore keeps ws_objects/ out of the build context, so such a read would
    fail in a container and in CI even where it happened to work locally.

    PROVENANCE: A CLEAN CREATION, NOT A TRANSLATED BUILD FILE
    PowerBuilder has no namespaces and no import statements (AAP §0.4.5.1); symbol resolution comes
    from the ordered library list in the target file, and ProjectReference has no ordering analogue,
    so that ordering is deliberately not encoded. The two PowerBuilder project objects are not
    translated either: AAP §0.8.6 R5 records that they disagree on library count and vendor and that
    both declare pfw.utility.imgcodec.pbl, which exists nowhere in the repository, so neither would
    build as written. This project file is what establishes PowerFramework.Shared.Localization as
    that namespace's compilation unit.

    GOVERNING CONSTRAINTS. review_rules reports "No user rules provided", so no user specified rule
    governs this file and none was invented. In their place AAP §0.7.2 (the enterprise baseline) and
    §0.7.3 (the twelve binding non rule constraints) apply. Structural authorities: §0.3.1 names this
    file, §0.5.4.3 classifies every project file as a CREATE, §0.3.2.1 fixes the validated build
    mechanism, and §0.5.4.1 makes central package management mandatory rather than optional.

    DELIBERATELY NOT DECLARED HERE, because every one is inherited by MSBuild directory walk up from
    the repository root Directory.Build.props, the single point of control for EVERY project in this
    repository: the six shared libraries, their sibling test projects, the four Phase 1 services and
    the service test projects alike. No count is quoted on purpose, because the roster grows as the
    tree is filled in and a numeral here would go stale silently. There is no intervening
    Directory.Build.props under shared/, so the walk up from this directory reaches the repository
    root and stops there, which is what makes that file the sole point of control:

        TargetFramework net10.0, LangVersion, Nullable enable, ImplicitUsings enable,
        TreatWarningsAsErrors true, EnableNETAnalyzers, AnalysisLevel,
        ManagePackageVersionsCentrally true, Deterministic, ContinuousIntegrationBuild,
        Product, Company, Copyright.

    Those names appear immediately above as documentation and nowhere else: not one of them is
    declared in this file. Restating any of them would be a defect even where the value happened to
    match, because it silently decouples this project from that single point of control, which is the
    seam through which one project drifts from the rest (AAP §0.7.3 C-I). Nullable reference types
    and warnings as errors therefore apply here in full, and no NoWarn blanket softens them.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Both values equal the defaults MSBuild derives from this file name, and are stated anyway so
         that a future directory rename cannot silently change the namespace and assembly identity
         that the .cs files here, the sibling test project and the consuming services all resolve
         against. The string is fixed by the AAP §0.4.5.1 namespace scheme
         PowerFramework.Shared.{Kernel, Diagnostics, Eventful, Localization, Containers} and must
         stay exactly this: shared/PowerFramework.Shared.Localization.Tests,
         services/gateway-service/PowerFramework.Gateway and
         services/dataservices-service/PowerFramework.DataServices each reference this project by
         this exact path, and the produced assembly must be
         PowerFramework.Shared.Localization.dll. -->
    <RootNamespace>PowerFramework.Shared.Localization</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>PowerFramework.Shared.Localization</AssemblyName>
    <Description>PowerFramework shared localization surface: the I18N entry points with their silent passthrough fallback, the translation categories, and the English, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese providers read from pfw.i18n.xml. Ported from the pfw.ui and pfw.ui.controls.ext i18n objects, mistranslations included.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="Project references: exactly one, and it must stay that way">
    <!--
      Constraint discharged here: AAP §0.7.3 C-I, each service builds and tests independently.

      Kernel is the SOLE dependency of this library, and that is a measured finding rather than a
      convention. ws_objects/pfw.ui.pbl.src/i18n.srf returns RetCode.E_INVALID_OBJECT and RetCode.OK
      and gates on IsValid before dispatching; it passes Enums.I18N_SRC_PFW as the default source;
      and ws_objects/pfw.ui.controls.ext.pbl.src/ne_cst_i18n.sru:L16-L17 derives CAT_MSGBOX and
      CAT_DWSVC from Enums.I18N_CAT_CUSTOM, declared at
      ws_objects/pfw.shared.pbl.src/enums.sru:L123 alongside I18N_CAT_WINDOW through
      I18N_CAT_DATAWINDOW. RetCode, Enums and Predicates.IsValidObject all land in
      PowerFramework.Shared.Kernel, so the algebra and the constant catalogue are preserved by REUSE
      and never reimplemented locally where they could drift from the values every other project
      shares.

      C-I also bounds this list. Nothing outside shared/ may be referenced, and within shared/
      nothing but Kernel: no PowerFramework.Contracts (that is the published boundary, not shared
      implementation), no other PowerFramework.Shared.* project, and nothing under services/.
      In particular NO reference to any Documents XML object family: AAP §0.2.1.3 Correction 6
      records that the concrete providers read the translation table with the DEFERRED Documents XML
      parser (n_cst_i18n_en.sru:L13 declares n_xmldoc, n_cst_i18n_cht.sru uses n_xmlqueryresult), and
      the resolution is to SUBSTITUTE System.Xml.Linq.XDocument.Load plus XPathSelectElements so that
      Localization acquires no Documents coupling and the XML family stays deferred. Nor may any of
      the four deferred services (DesignSystem, Documents, Integration, ScriptBridge) be named: AAP
      §0.2.2.2 forbids implementing them even as a stub, so they have no project to reference.
      Relative path only: never an absolute path, and never a package standing in for a project.

      Left deliberately public rather than hidden behind PrivateAssets. The sibling test project
      takes no direct Kernel reference of its own and reaches RetCode, Enums and Predicates
      transitively through this edge, so narrowing it would break that project.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\PowerFramework.Shared.Kernel\PowerFramework.Shared.Kernel.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    ZERO PackageReference elements, and zero is the correct count (AAP §0.7.3 C-A, §0.5.3).

    The substitution named in AAP §0.2.1.3 Correction 6 and §0.4.2.3 is System.Xml.Linq.XDocument
    with XPathSelectElements, and both ship inside the Microsoft.NETCore.App shared framework that
    net10.0 already targets, so the reader needs no package at all. Nothing else here performs I/O,
    networking, logging, serialization or database access, so no ASP.NET reference, no web SDK and no
    third party package belongs in this project; §0.5.3 additionally rules out adding a localization
    or resource framework, because the three providers are ported logic with exact legacy semantics
    (including the two mistranslations and the no op Simplified Chinese provider) rather than a
    resource strategy to be re-expressed.

    Do not add a package "to be safe": an unnecessary reference drags a NuGet audit surface onto a
    library that two in scope services depend on. If one ever does become genuinely necessary, add
    it VERSIONLESS and pin the version in the repository root Directory.Packages.props.
    ManagePackageVersionsCentrally is enabled repository wide (AAP §0.5.4.1), so an inline Version
    attribute here is a restore error (NU1008) rather than a shortcut, and a floating, wildcard or
    "latest" version is barred outright by the §0.7.2 baseline. Because this project declares no
    package, no NU1903 advisory can originate in it; one appearing at restore arrived transitively
    through Kernel and must be reported, never suppressed from here.
  -->

  <!--
    Also deliberately absent, each for a stated reason, so the omissions read as decisions:

      * Any item naming pfw.i18n.xml. The translation table is a repository root data file that the
        root .dockerignore explicitly re-includes (!pfw.i18n.xml) so it survives into the build
        context, and the sibling test project links its own copy with CopyToOutputDirectory. How the
        table reaches a running service - linked content here, embedded resource, or a path supplied
        through configuration - is a delivery decision that belongs with I18nResourceReader.cs and
        the consuming services' settings, not with this project file, and stating it here would
        pre-empt it. Note the file is READ ONLY legacy data either way (AAP §0.2.1.2): it is read as
        the resource table and never edited.
      * OutputType. This is a class library and must stay one; the SDK default of Library is correct.
        The Exe value belongs ONLY to the hand authored xunit.v3 test projects, which fail to build
        without it. Setting it here would turn a library into an application and break every
        consumer.
      * EnableDefaultCompileItems, and any explicit Compile, Content, None, EmbeddedResource or
        Remove item. SDK style projects glob the .cs files in this directory automatically and they
        all sit flat here, so there is nothing to add and nothing to exclude. An explicit list would
        be worse than redundant: it would silently drop any file added later.
      * InternalsVisibleTo. The legacy objects are global classes whose whole surface is called from
        other objects, so every ported type and member is public and the sibling test project and the
        consuming services reach all of it without one.
      * NoWarn, WarningsNotAsErrors and any project wide analyzer suppression. The only suppressions
        this refactor needs are the naming ones for the preserved SCREAMING_SNAKE constant
        identifiers such as CAT_MSGBOX and CAT_DWSVC, and AAP §0.4.5.3 keeps those file glob scoped
        in the repository root .editorconfig. A suppression here would broaden that scope to this
        whole project.
      * GenerateDocumentationFile. Inherited TreatWarningsAsErrors turns a missing XML documentation
        comment (CS1591) into a build error, and no requirement asks for a documentation file.
      * PackageId, Version, IsPackable, GeneratePackageOnBuild and all other packaging metadata.
        Nothing in this refactor publishes these libraries as NuGet packages; they are consumed by
        ProjectReference, and the shipped artifacts are four container images, one per in scope
        service.
      * Any solution filter. .NET 10 emits the XML .slnx solution format and legacy .slnf filters are
        incompatible with it, failing with MSB4014 during restore, build and test (AAP §0.3.2.1).
        Build scoping is done by the per service .slnx files together with the root property sheets.
  -->

</Project>
